# Huffman_Codification_Algorithm_Demonstration

Academic project developed to simulate the Huffman coding algorithm using Python and Tkinter.

## Description

This application demonstrates the Huffman coding algorithm, a lossless data compression technique that assigns variable-length binary codes to characters based on their frequency.

The project aims to provide a visual representation of the algorithm and facilitate the understanding of its main steps.

## Technologies

- Python
- Tkinter

## Algorithm

The Huffman coding algorithm follows these steps:

1. Calculate the frequency of each character.
2. Build a Huffman tree based on character frequencies.
3. Generate binary codes by travelling the tree.
4. Encode the input using the generated codes.

## Execution

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Madakase/Huffman_Codification_Algorithm_Demonstration.git
```

Navigate to the project directory:

```bash
cd Huffman_Codification_Algorithm_Demonstration
```

Run the application:

```bash
python main.py
```

## Academic Purpose

This project was developed to study and demonstrate the Huffman coding algorithm, its implementation, and its application to lossless data compression.
